body:
Hi @jthcc we currently only supports giving a template per hits.

We are thinking about giving the users the possibility to provide their own full hits template (so you will have to iterate yourself the hits in the template).

We are not sure right now this would be the best solution.

In the meantime what you can do is create a custom widget:

```js
var myHitsWidget = {
  _container: $('#myHits'),
  getConfiguration: function() {
    return {
      hitsPerPage: 50
    }
  },
  init: function() {
    // if you need some jQuery code here, do it
  },
  render: function(args) {
    var out = '';
    args.results.hits.forEach(function(hit) {
      out += '...'; // do whatever you want here, any html structure
    });
    this._container.html(html);
  }
};

search.addWidget(myHitsWidget);
```
